\section*{The joint GFF and cluster limit of critical Ashkin–Teller currents}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Along the critical Ashkin--Teller line, the height and both nested current-cluster systems are claimed to converge jointly to one Gaussian field and its canonical recursive two-valued local sets.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} Fix \(J>0,U\le J\) on \(\sinh(2J)=e^{-2U}\), and set \(t=(1+e^{4U})^{-1/2}\), \(c=1/t\), \(g=8\arcsin(c/2)/\pi\), \(a=\pi\sqrt g/2\). In a bounded Jordan domain with uniformly approximating simple lattice polygons, use the specified wired-primal/free-dual Ashkin--Teller current coupling: spin pairs have no simultaneous primal/dual disagreement and weight \(t^{N(\tau)+N(\tau^\dagger)}\); when neither disagrees, edge states \((1,0),(0,1),(0,0)\) have probabilities \(1-t,1-t,2t-1\). The height is pinned zero on the boundary and has corner increments \(\tfrac12\tau(v)\tau^\dagger(f)\). The claimed joint limit is
\[
 (H_\delta,\mathcal C_\delta^{\mathrm w},\mathcal C_\delta^{\mathrm f},C_{\partial,\delta})
 \Longrightarrow(h/(\pi\sqrt g),\mathcal C^{\mathrm w},\mathcal C^{\mathrm f},A_{-a,a}(h)).
\]
Here \(h\) is the zero-boundary GFF with logarithmic singularity \(-\log|z-w|\), and \(A_{-a,a}\) is its canonical two-valued local set. The continuum wired/free cluster families are the recursive local-set constructions from this same \(h\). Heights converge locally in \(H^s\), \(s<-1\); cluster matching and the distinguished boundary component use Hausdorff geometry, retaining every positive-diameter cluster. Conditional on spins, different edge-pair samples are independent. Dual disagreement forces the edge pair $(1,0)$, and primal disagreement forces $(0,1)$. Primal spins are fixed to $+1$ on the boundary, the boundary-cycle primal edges are open, and dual boundary spins are free. The height distribution is smeared atomically:
\[
 H_\delta(\varphi)=\delta^2\sum_{v\in V_\delta}H_\delta(v)\varphi(v).
\]

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Exact cuts and spatial comparisons establish reflection-positive covariance and Gaussian Laplace screening. Stopped local-set exploration keeps the current clusters coupled to the same field, and iteration retains every nesting level together with the wired boundary cluster, including the four-state endpoint.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Along the critical Ashkin--Teller line, the height and both nested current-cluster systems are claimed to converge jointly to one Gaussian field and its canonical recursive two-valued local sets. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

